            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_a68e36cc">
               <extent xml:id="extent_e4170796">2 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_1e19ca26">25 x 20</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_937fcf89">Framed in glass on both sides. Written in ink. Paper: 11 staves. Above the music Gade has written:<lb xml:id="idm36"/>Lyksalig den, som ydmygt troer,<lb xml:id="idm37"/>Hvad Øiet ei kan gjætte!<lb xml:id="idm38"/>Naar Christi Lys i Sjælen boer,<lb xml:id="idm39"/>Han træffer dog det Rette.<lb xml:id="idm40"/>Written in chorale notation with the text above the first stave. At the end of the music dated "Kjøbenhavn d 24 Juni / 1862." At the bottom of the page Gade has written: "Min kjære Søster Marie til venlig Erindring / om Niels W. Gade" (My dear sister Marie in kind remembrance of Niels W. Gade). On the verso written in pencil in unknown hand: "Presented from N. Gade to his sister Mary Nov. 6th 1868"</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
